    {
      "id": "CIM-03",
      "chapter": "normalization",
      "title": "The integral height-two parameter and its inverse",
      "anchor": "normalization-cm-inert-parameter",
      "statement": "At an inert prime p≥5 the selected CM3 theorem yields a unit ε in the completed unramified field for which Θ=e_E(εℓ) has integral coefficients, where e_E is the curve formal exponential and ℓ=Σ T^(p^(2j))/p^j. The inverse of Θ is defined over the same integer ring and satisfies ℓ∘Θ⁻¹=ε⁻¹L_E.",
